        "name": "Juno 0.1.5",
        "notes": "# No developer tools popup, and lighter, faster runs\n\n## What's new\n\n- No more \"install the command line developer tools\" popup: on a Mac without Apple's developer tools, Juno never starts git or the other tools that would ask for them. If a task needs git, Juno says it is not installed instead.\n- Lighter runs: Juno's instructions are shorter and clearer, so each task uses about a third fewer tokens with the same results. The checks that keep you safe moved into code, where they always hold: a \"prove you're human\" check is never pressed through, Juno never asks you for a password in the chat, and an identity detail from your memory stays masked.\n\n## Fixes\n\n- A form whose only sign of success is a popup message is now seen as sent, not as \"nothing was done\".\n- Choices drawn as pictures, like stars or icons over hidden buttons, can now be picked.\n- A file attached to a form shows its name, so Juno can tell it is there.",
